The café is very crowded.
I hold my bag securely.
I look everywhere.
I need an empty seat.
There is a small table near the window.
One chair is empty there.
There is an elderly man at the neighboring table.
I ask him.
"Kaka, is this seat available?"
The elderly man smiles and says, "Yes, madam."
I say "Thank you" to him.
I sit on that wooden chair.
I keep my bag near me.
I look up.
There are large fans on the ceiling.
Those old fans turn slowly.
The atmosphere here is very pleasant.
I like this old place a lot.
I look outside through the window.
Now I wait for my tea.
